{"outcome":"undetermined","route_plan":[{"requirement_ref":"region_a:sender_lawful_ground","route":"Specific consent"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:recipient_lawful_ground","route":"Specific consent"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:consent_conditions","route":"met"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:sender_sensitive_processing","route":"Health-care processing by a professional subject to secrecy"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:recipient_sensitive_processing","route":"Explicit consent"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:outward_transfer_route","route":"Approved transfer clauses"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:a1_healthcare_processing","route":"Processing directly by or under the responsibility of a registered A1 practitioner"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:a1_professional_secrecy","route":"Disclosure with the patient's consent"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:a1_genetic_transfer_restriction","route":"A lawful outward-transfer route not based on Article 19(1)(a)"}],"reasoning":"Region A applies to Kestrel's processing because it is established in Subregion A1, and to Harrow's processing because the recipient offers care to a person in Region A (f_12d62771fdeb, f_cbbbb15c04e0; A-REG 3#L1, A-REG 3#L2). The data is identified personal information and includes health and genetic information, so it is sensitive information (f_6fcc5cd6b927, f_72bdc3d5c28e, f_7892b94ae5e8; A-REG 4#L2, A-REG 4#L3, A-REG 4#L4, A-REG 4#L5). The stated clinical second-opinion purpose, the registered A1 practitioners, and the patient's written consent support the processing, lawful-ground, sensitive-processing, secrecy, and consent-condition requirements (f_987ab471487e, f_110e981b0a7c, f_5ec21466d488, f_66d5f3ce3996, f_e22033e7c743; A-REG 6#L1, A-REG 6#L2, A-REG 7#L1, A-REG 8#L2, A-REG 8#L3, A-REG 8#L5, A1-HIA 4#L1, A1-HIA 5#L1, A1-HIA 5#L2). The consent therefore remains useful for processing and permitted disclosure, even though it cannot itself supply the outward-transfer route.

Making the information available to Harrow in Region B is an outward transfer (f_5aa17aaaa329, f_73d3eb94625a; A-REG 4#L10). Recognition is unavailable because Region B recognition is limited both to active certified recipients and to non-sensitive information; Harrow has no certification and the information is sensitive (f_febc895bce9, f_72bdc3d5c28e, f_7892b94ae5e8; A-REG 17#L1, A-REG 17#L2, A-REG 17#L3, A-REG Annex II#L1). The proposed consent route is also unavailable for the genetic report because A1 law expressly prohibits making genetic information the subject of an outward transfer on the basis of Article 19(1)(a) (f_55ec68a77a25, f_6a3e2263dd33; A-REG 19#L1, A-REG 19#L2, A-REG 19#L6, A1-HIA 7#L1). This is compatible with using consent for the separate processing and secrecy requirements.

The coherent alternative is Article 18: execute approved transfer clauses, assess Region B law and practice concerning public-authority access or disclosure, and adopt supplementary measures where necessary (f_d75ec85c160f; A-REG 16#L1, A-REG 18#L1, A-REG 18#L2). If effective supplementary measures cannot be adopted, the transfer cannot proceed on that route (A-REG 18#L3). The required Region B answer remains open, so the outward-transfer gate and the A1 genetic-transfer gate cannot yet be finally decided. The A1 hosting/storage conditions are not engaged because Harrow keeps the information in its own clinical record for its own care rather than hosting Kestrel's records (f_3707d0e0f8a9, f_7ddb7b6d46db, f_a7a94423ed89; A1-HIA 6#L1, A1-HIA 6#L4). The A1 listed impact-assessment triggers are likewise not engaged, but Article 12(1)'s independent high-risk requirement remains unresolved (f_7e86304fe561, f_e77bee462e0e; A1-HIA 8#L1, A1-HIA 8#L2, A1-HIA 8#L3, A-REG 12#L1, A-REG 12#L2, A-REG 12#L3, A-REG 12#L4, A-REG 12#L5, A-REG 12#L6).","quote_ids":["A-REG 3#L1","A-REG 3#L2","A-REG 4#L2","A-REG 4#L3","A-REG 4#L4","A-REG 4#L5","A-REG 4#L10","A-REG 5#L1","A-REG 5#L2","A-REG 5#L3","A-REG 5#L4","A-REG 5#L5","A-REG 5#L6","A-REG 5#L7","A-REG 6#L1","A-REG 6#L2","A-REG 7#L1","A-REG 8#L1","A-REG 8#L2","A-REG 8#L3","A-REG 8#L5","A-REG 12#L1","A-REG 12#L2","A-REG 12#L3","A-REG 12#L4","A-REG 12#L5","A-REG 12#L6","A-REG 13#L1","A-REG 14#L1","A-REG 16#L1","A-REG 17#L1","A-REG 17#L2","A-REG 17#L3","A-REG 18#L1","A-REG 18#L2","A-REG 18#L3","A-REG 19#L1","A-REG 19#L2","A-REG 19#L6","A-REG Annex II#L1","A1-HIA 4#L1","A1-HIA 5#L1","A1-HIA 5#L2","A1-HIA 6#L1","A1-HIA 6#L3","A1-HIA 6#L4","A1-HIA 7#L1","A1-HIA 8#L1","A1-HIA 8#L2","A1-HIA 8#L3"],"conflicts":[],"summary":"The transfer is not permitted as described because consent cannot be used as the outward-transfer basis for the genetic report. It may be satisfiable through approved transfer clauses, but the Region B public-authority-access answer and the independent Article 12(1) high-risk determination remain unresolved.","blockers":[{"requirement_ref":"region_a:outward_transfer_route","gap":"The only selected route that can accommodate the genetic component is Article 18, but the required answer on Region B law and practice concerning public-authority access or disclosure to Harrow is still missing. Without that answer, the Article 18(2) assessment and any necessary supplementary measures cannot be determined.","why_not_a_confirmation":"Confirming that the patient gave risk-informed consent does not resolve this gap: Article 18 requires a separate third-territory law-and-practice assessment, and consent is unavailable for the genetic outward transfer under A1-HIA 7."},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:a1_genetic_transfer_restriction","gap":"The proposed Article 19(1)(a) route is expressly unavailable for the genetic information, and no lawful non-Article 19(1)(a) route has yet been established. The proposed transfer therefore cannot be decided as lawful until the Article 18 alternative is completed or another lawful route is established.","why_not_a_confirmation":"Further confirmation of the existing consent cannot cure the express A1 restriction; the missing item is a different lawful outward-transfer basis."},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:impact_assessment","gap":"No documented determination has been made under Article 12(1) as to whether this identified genetic and health-information processing is likely to result in a high risk to the patient's rights. Without that determination, it cannot be decided whether a pre-processing impact assessment is required.","why_not_a_confirmation":"The fact that the A1 list-based triggers are absent does not resolve Article 12(1)'s independent high-risk test."}],"notes":["The current Region B finding is that the Region B Health Records Act and Records Access Act do not apply to Harrow or Kestrel on the supplied facts; no Region B gate is therefore engaged on that finding. The open Article 18 question nevertheless needs the Region B specialist's answer about any applicable public-authority access or disclosure powers and their effect on clause compliance.","If Article 18 is pursued, the parties must execute the approved transfer clauses, complete the Article 18(2) assessment, adopt necessary supplementary measures, and stop if effective supplementary measures cannot be adopted.","The one-off nature of the referral supports the occasional-transfer condition for Article 19(1)(a) and (b), but does not overcome the A1 genetic-information restriction (f_2f7b22f9f431; A-REG 19#L6).","The clinics should create or update the written processing records required by Article 13 and document risk-appropriate technical and organisational security measures and regular testing under Article 14. The encrypted upload is relevant but does not by itself establish all Article 14 measures (f_8c44c6e413c5; A-REG 13#L1, A-REG 14#L1).","Recognition, the contract derogation, and the public-interest derogation are not selected routes. The supplied facts do not establish recognition, a qualifying contract necessity, or an applicable public-interest basis (f_febc895bce9, f_d75ec85c160f; A-REG 17#L3, A-REG 19#L3, A-REG 19#L5)."],"routings":[{"question_ref":"region_a:q1","to_corpus":"region_b","question":"Under the Region B law and practice assessed for Harrow, does any public authority have power to require Harrow to disclose or permit access to the transferred clinical information, and would that power prevent Harrow from complying with approved Article 18 transfer clauses or require supplementary measures?"}],"corrections":[]}

