   "applicability": "The supplied information is a health record under B-HRA 2 because it identifies an individual and relates to physical health and the provision of health care. But B-HRA 3 limits Sections 4\u20138 to covered providers and service agents, and Section 9 to data hosts. Harrow is not a covered provider because it does not bill a Region B-licensed health insurer and is not an insurer. It is not a service agent because it maintains the information in its own clinical record for its own care, rather than on behalf of a covered provider, and it is not a data host because it stores no records on behalf of another person. The sender is likewise not shown to be a covered provider or service agent. Harrow is also not shown to be a computing provider under B-RAA 2; it is a clinic using its own clinical referral portal, not a provider of storage, hosting or computing services.",
